            <ArticleTitle>Acute right coronary artery embolus after aortic valve surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>367-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 35-year-old man with rheumatic aortic valve regurgitation developed acute right ventricular failure 8 days after valve replacement with a mechanical prosthesis. Angiography showed a right coronary artery embolus. Successful coronary artery bypass grafting was performed on the beating heart.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
